  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Aas Khan@Aas Mohammad vs State Of Rajasthan Through Pp on 3 January, 2018 Author: Pankaj Bhandari Bench: Pankaj Bhandari High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous Anticipatory Bail No.12091/2017 Aas Khan @ Aas Mohammad S/o Pratap B/c Mev, R/o Village Gaondi, Police Station Jurhara, Distt. Bharatpur (raj.) ----Petitioner Versus State of Rajasthan Through P.P. ----Respondent _____________________________________________________ For Petitioner(s) : Mr.Azad Khan. F o r R e s p o n d e n t ( s ) : M r . S u d e s h S a i n i , P P . _____________________________________________________ Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Pankaj Bhandari Order 03/01/2018",
    "facts": "1. Petitioner has filed this miscellaneous bail application under Section 438 Cr.P.C. 2. F.I.R. No.218/2017 was registered at Police Station Kaman, District Bharatpur for offence under Sections 420, 272 of I.P.C. and Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006.",
    "arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that offences under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 as well as offences under Sections 272 of IPC are bailable and Section 420 of IPC has been added to make it a non-bailable offence. 4. Learned Public Prosecutor has opposed the bail application.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. It is contended by counsel for the petitioner that offences under Sections 58, 59 of Food Safety and Standard Act, 2006 as well as offences under Sections 272 of IPC are bailable and Section 420 of IPC has been added to make it a non-bailable offence. 4.",
    "respondent_arguments": "Learned Public Prosecutor has opposed the bail application.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
